# Session slots and focus

## Model

- Apps are real processes bound to a slot (`ag_session_bind_to`), not parked builtins.
- `run` / `fm` pin the launch slot, spawn with `AG_SPAWN_NO_SESSION`, then bind.
- AXE load is deferred in `proc_task` (`AG_PS_LOADING`); shell must not block on HostFS.

## Focus rules

- Ready app owns the screen: **no** console banner on focus (overpaints FM/AMP).
- Same-slot bind (`shell → app`) must still set foreground + `FOCUS_GAINED` (adopt path).
- While `AG_PS_LOADING`, focus must show `enter_loading_view` — otherwise Alt-back looks hung.
- Unfocused apps: no console writes; `ag_poll_event` must sleep on timeout (no busy-spin).
- Ignore `QUIT` while unfocused (shell injects QUIT only for its own prompt).

## Keyboard

- `ag_session_shell_owns_keyboard` is true only when focused slot pid is kernel.
- Alt+1..4 / Ctrl+\ are supervisor hotkeys; they work even when an app owns the slot.

## Do not

- Defer bind until load finishes (reopens Alt race into the wrong slot).
- Restore a generic “focused app” console banner for ready apps.
